@startuml
title MODRISS Integrated Product Lifecycle — Two Coordinated Processes
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity { BackgroundColor #FCFBF7; BorderColor #617178; FontColor #102C3A; DiamondBackgroundColor #D7E9E5; DiamondBorderColor #087B78 }

|Development and Delivery|
start
:Phase 0 — Inception, Tailoring & Organization\n«Activity, Phase; occurs once»;
if (G0/G1 authorized?) then (yes)
else (redirect / stop)
  stop
endif

:Phase 1 — Active Product Construction & Evolution\n«Activity, Phase; occurs once»;
repeat
  repeat
    :Model-driven increment iteration\nvertical slice; G2–G5\n«Activity, Iteration»;
  repeat while (Another increment?) is (yes)
  :Release and transition activities\nqualify, promote, hand over; G6–G7\n«Activity»;
  if (Candidate or promotion rejected?) then (yes)
    :Retain accepted baseline; route correction\nto earliest authoritative source;
  else (accepted)
    :First accepted release is ready for G7 handover;
  endif
repeat while (First release accepted at G7?) is (rework)
:G7 hands the first accepted release to Operations and Maintenance;

fork
  while (Next release selected and retirement not authorized?) is (next release)
    :Run another model-driven increment and release iteration;
    :G7 updates the accepted live-release set;
  endwhile (retirement authorized)
  :Phase 2 — Retire, Migrate & Close\n«Activity, Phase; occurs once»;
  :Contribute Development and Delivery closure evidence to shared G8;
fork again
  |Operations and Maintenance|
  :Start the ongoing process at first G7;
  repeat
    :Operate & observe live release;
    :Kanban service delivery\nRequested → Ready → In Progress → Verify → Done;
    :Respond to incident/problem or maintain;
    if (Product change?) then (yes)
      |Development and Delivery|
      :Route to earliest authoritative source\nand applicable release controls;
      |Operations and Maintenance|
    else (operations-only)
    endif
    :Verify, reconcile and learn;
  repeat while (Any live release remains?) is (yes)
  :Contribute operational shutdown evidence to shared G8;
end fork

|Development and Delivery|
:G8 — accept shared closure evidence\nonly when no live release remains;
stop

legend bottom
  Phase = bounded sequential period ending at a major checkpoint.
  The three phases occur once; only Phase 1 activities and iterations repeat.
  Operations and Maintenance = ongoing, event-driven Process, not a Phase.
  DevOps coordinates G7 handover, CI/CD, telemetry, change and evidence.
  G8 is a shared closure criterion, not an activity-flow edge between the processes.
endlegend
@enduml
